senses.gloss:
कब(व)न्धिन् a. ‘Endowed with water’, epithet of the Maruts;
 अर्यमणो न मरुतः कबन्धिनः Rv. 5. 54. 8. ━m. N. of Kātyāyana.
 कबन्धी कात्यायनः पप्रच्छ Praśna. Up. 1. 1.

कवारि^1 a. Ved. Selfish, stingy; a mean or contemptible enemy;
 न कवारिभ्यो न हि ते पृणन्ति Rv. 10. 107. 3.
[1] Correction submitted by on 20170124. note: the adj. in -ī is improbable.

कव(ब)र + .{@-रः, -रम्@}
—1 Salt.
—2 Sourness or acidity.

कव(ब)र + .{@-रः@}
—1 A braid or fillet of hair.
—2 A lecturer (पाठक).

कव(ब)र + .{@-रः, -रम्@}
—1 Salt.
—2 Sourness or acidity.

कवष, -कवष् + .{@-षः@}
—1 A shield.
—2 N. of a Ṛṣi (कवष ऐलूष); Rv. 7. 18. 12.

काव्य + .{@-व्या@}
—1 Intelligence.
—2 A female fiend;
